# Owo 2.5 — findings by Qwen 3.8 Flash (self-excluded: unattributed codename, no verified model of that name)

## Exclusion note

**No scores are asserted for `owo-2.5`.** As of 2026-10-23 there is **no identifiable AI model named "Owo 2.5"** from any lab, product, or benchmark aggregator. It carries only a **scaffolded `meta.json`** ("Owo 2.5 model evaluation entry / 128K / Text in/out / Standard pricing") with no provider, repo, or product page. A direct check of the **live OpenRouter "Stealth" model roster** shows the current anonymous slots are exactly **`stealth/ox-alpha`, `stealth/space-bunny-alpha`, and `stealth/union-alpha`** — **`owo-2.5` is not among them**. Every web sweep for "Owo 2.5" as an LLM resolves only to noise: OCR garble from an unrelated scanned yearbook, the **"OwO"** roleplay/internet meme, the **"OwQ"** *outlier-aware weight-quantization* **method** (a technique, not a model), and **QwQ** chatter. There is **no first-party model card, no tech report, no Artificial Analysis / OpenRouter / Vals row, and no independent press** for an LLM called Owo 2.5. Per `RULES.md` (research permanence + no-fabrication + no-reattribution), this is **excluded**, not scored.

### Why this is an exclusion rather than a score

- **Not in the real stealth roster.** The genuine OpenRouter/OpenCode anonymous aliases (ox-alpha → de-anonymized to GLM-5.3-Flash; space-bunny-alpha; union-alpha) each have documented footprints and, in two cases, **their own folders here**. `owo-2.5` matches **none** of them and has **no listing** on the stealth endpoint — so it is not even a corroborated anonymous model.
- **No identity anchor.** Unlike a freshly-shipped short-named real model (Flint — resolvable to Recursive Intelligence with a launch date, HF repo and press), Owo 2.5 resolves to **no maker or product** at all.
- **Name-collisions are not evidence.** "OwQ" is a **quantization method** and "OwO" is a **meme**, not this model; treating either as Owo 2.5's identity would be **fabrication**. Attributing it to a guessed parent (e.g. an ox-alpha/space-bunny/union sibling) is likewise forbidden **reattribution**.
- **Zero capability data.** The scaffold's "128K / text / Standard pricing" is generic placeholder boilerplate, uncorroborated by any source, with no benchmark absolute to normalize against.

